    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0384" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.24/255</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)<anchor n="4" xml:id="d357-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-15">December 15, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sr. García Arias, Minister of the Argentine Embassy, called to state that his
                    Government desired either the Ambassador or, in the Ambassador’s absence, his
                    representative to participate in the discussions which will take place between
                    the Argentine Military and Naval Commission<anchor n="5" xml:id="d357-f2"/> and
                    the military and naval authorities of this Government. Sr. García Arias
                    requested that his Government’s desire be brought to the attention of the proper
                    authorities in our War and Navy Departments so that they would not be surprised
                    by the participation of the Ambassador or his representative in the
                    discussions.</p>
                <p>I said this would be done.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Liaison Officer (Wilson) and the Under Secretary of State
                    (Welles).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f2" n="5" xml:id="d357-f2-content">
                <p>The Commission consisted of five military officers headed by Brig. Gen. Eduardo
                    T. Lapez and six naval officers under Rear Adm. Sabá Sueyro.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
